      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: validate repository size from index blobs",
        "body": "## Summary\n- inspect tracked Git index blobs instead of mutable working-tree files\n- reject oversized staged content even when the working copy changed or disappeared\n- handle a fresh repository with an empty index without an unbound-array failure\n- reject release/build artifacts across app, dSYM, xcarchive, xcresult, ipa, zip, delta, dmg, pkg, tar.gz, and tgz forms\n- cover the exact 2 MiB boundary, empty indexes, submodule gitlinks, symlinks, staged deletions, and newline-containing paths\n- keep one-suite macOS shard isolation while allowing Intel cold builds enough time to compile the full test target\n\nFollow-up hardening for #1858. Preserves contributor credit in the changelog.\n\n## Proof\n- Exact head: `d70e367fd136eacadb510544c852854ddb7935e5`.\n- `Scripts/test_repository_size.sh`: passed, including empty index and staged-vs-working-tree cases.\n- `Scripts/check_repository_size.sh`: passed against the repository index.\n- `shellcheck Scripts/check_repository_size.sh Scripts/test_repository_size.sh`: passed.\n- `Scripts/test_ci_path_gate.sh`: passed.\n- `make check`: all repository guards, documentation, locale, SwiftFormat, and SwiftLint checks passed; zero lint violations.\n- `make test`: all 46/46 shards passed on the implementation head; the exact-head CI run is authoritative for the timeout-only follow-up.\n- Exact-head autoreview: clean, 0.90 correctness, no accepted/actionable findings.\n\nThe first Intel shard spent about 26 minutes compiling, passed 64 isolated suites, then hit the previous 35-minute step timeout without a test failure. The new 50-minute step / 60-minute job budgets preserve the existing per-suite timeout and isolation.\n\n## Risk\nLow. The change is isolated to repository-maintenance shell scripts, documentation, and CI time budgets; it does not alter the app or release artifacts.",
